{# The key must match relayhost exactly, brackets included: postfix looks up
   the nexthop as written, so "smtp.gmail.com:587" never matches a relayhost of
   "[smtp.gmail.com]:587" -- it simply finds no credential, skips AUTH, and
   Gmail answers "Authentication Required" at MAIL FROM.

   Gmail shows an app password as four groups of four -- "abcd efgh ijkl mnop"
   -- but the password is the sixteen characters; the spaces are display only.
   They are stripped here because this file is whitespace-delimited, so a
   password containing them would be parsed as the wrong fields entirely. The
   same strip is applied wherever else this entry is used, or the two would
   authenticate with different strings. #}
[{{ pve_mail_relay_host }}]:{{ pve_mail_relay_port }} {{ pve_mail_username }}:{{ lookup('keepass', pve_mail_password_entry) | replace(' ', '') }}
